From 55c7d7799e435f7fd189d5b5c2926bd88116b2b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Devesh Rai <devesh.rai@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:31:11 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 40/46] Android: fixes from a crash hunt on the tablet

Launchers: the Gerber Viewer, the calculator tools and the drawing sheet
editor are started in-process from COMMON_CONTROL::Execute(), as there is
no executable to run on Android ("Command could not be found").  The
calculator frame keeps the maximized state that LoadWindowState() gave it,
and the Gerber viewer handles wxID_CLOSE, which is what its File menu has
when it runs in the project manager's process.

Frames shown with KIWAY_PLAYER::ShowModal() are maximized like every other
frame; the footprint chooser, which loads no window state, opened at its
fitted size in the top left corner, over the menu bar.  Its filter box now
has the focus when it opens, and the caller's canvas gets the focus back
when a modal frame closes: with touch there is no pointer to hover over
the canvas, and the hotkeys were dead until it was tapped.

3D viewer: make the frame opaque before swapping buffers.  After the app
had been in the background the board body was see-through and showed the
window behind it.

MCP: kicad_open_editor rejects editor names other than "pcb" and
"schematic" instead of opening the board editor for them.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
